# The contracts/ trust anchor is SHA256SUMS.minisig — and there must be exactly
# ONE of it. On 2026-07-26 two conflicting copies existed at once: the tracked
# signature (trusted comment 2026-07-17, verifies) and an untracked backup copy
# named SHA256SUMS.minisig.<suffix> (trusted comment 2026-07-15, does NOT
# verify). Whichever copy a `cp` or `tar` happens to pick decides what the
# offline consumer believes, which is the opposite of a trust anchor.
#
# `pl contracts verify` and `pl contracts bundle` now FAIL CLOSED with
# "AMBIGUOUS TRUST ANCHOR" when more than one contracts/*.minisig* exists. These
# rules stop a stray copy being committed in the first place.
#
# Do NOT add a broader rule here: contracts/*.schema.json, SHA256SUMS and
# SHA256SUMS.minisig are all tracked on purpose.
SHA256SUMS.minisig.*
*.minisig.bak
